#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147390 :question/id #uuid "d1946905-5833-58c2-9a0a-4dfd04eb922b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8963" :question/problem "The substitution $z=y^m$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} + x^3y= \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form $z'(x) + P(x)z(x) = Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} + p(x)y= q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x) = x^3, \\qquad q(x) = 1, \\qquad n=-\\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by $y^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\ny^{1/2} \\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} + x^3y^{3/2}= 1.\\qquad\\qquad (\\ast)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz= y^{1-n} =  y^{3/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = \\dfrac{3}{2}y^{1/2} \\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\ny^{1/2}\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{2}{3}\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(\\ast)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{3}\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + x^3\\,z = 1\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + \\dfrac{3}{2}x^3z = \\dfrac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x) = \\dfrac{3}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147391 :question/id #uuid "047ea3c1-8ebf-5e26-9f28-c5a87e7cf997" :question/math-academy-id "e-8965" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\dfrac{y}{x}  = \\dfrac{x^2}{y} .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} + p(x)y= q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x}, \\qquad q(x) = x^2, \\qquad n=-1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by $y^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\ny \\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} + \\dfrac{y^{2}}{x}= x^2.\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz= y^{1-n} =  y^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 2y \\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\ny\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + \\dfrac{1}{x}z  = x^2\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + \\dfrac{2}{x} z\n\t\t=2x^2\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=2{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x^2$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}z) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (2{x}^{2}) \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2xz & =2{x}^{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{2}) & =2{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{x}^{2} & =\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{2{x}^{5}+C}{5{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=5C_1.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z=y^{2}.$ This results in the general solution\n\n$$\ny^{ 2} =\\dfrac{2x^5 + C}{5x^2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147393 :question/id #uuid "b5189ec2-ea1c-5036-9543-b963bd072ab7" :question/math-academy-id "e-9069" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\n- $y\\,y' + x^2y^2 = e^x y^4$\n\n- $xy' + x^3y = -x^2 y^3$\n\n- $y' + y\\cos{x} = e^{y+1}$" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} + p(x)y= q(x)y^n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Bernoulli differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\ny' + x^2y = e^x y^3\n$$\n\nwhich is a Bernoulli differential equation with\n\n$$\np(x) = x^2, \\qquad q(x) = e^x, \\qquad n=3.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\ny' + x^2y = -xy^3\n$$\n\nwhich is a Bernoulli differential equation with\n\n$$\np(x) = x^2, \\qquad q(x) =-x, \\qquad n=3.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $q(x)y^n$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "186d0c19-d903-54ae-af08-d3ae1a5eb252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238262} {:answer/id #uuid "4aaf5040-9bb1-5f15-aaf3-d4836f0fc679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238700} {:answer/id #uuid "98d9b37c-f261-5386-aa13-02f5a695b4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239382} {:answer/id #uuid "b845640e-7864-59e9-85fd-ffdb6a89bfe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239660} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0ad406-2f7e-5d20-90a7-561a831321bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4aaf5040-9bb1-5f15-aaf3-d4836f0fc679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238700} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7ae302c-36a8-5375-ba5d-947ebfa7e674" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1480f672-8091-5903-a81e-b755f04694ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-106069" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some integer $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y=x{y}^{4}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)=x,\\,n=4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{-3}=x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-3{y}^{-4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}z=x\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}z=-3x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-3{x}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0152f8f7-2919-5e62-9d08-52bb7a0aa144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238092} {:answer/id #uuid "127581ed-48f8-548e-8e57-417c6d76c08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238209} {:answer/id #uuid "5588de14-4a7e-5282-8d89-7c4be377ce20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238794} {:answer/id #uuid "8b18979b-02a8-536d-a7e9-b6ee139da31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239263} {:answer/id #uuid "d69f1982-2eef-5f61-8533-78b91415f605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5588de14-4a7e-5282-8d89-7c4be377ce20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238794} :answer-field/id #uuid "e019cc4e-185b-5dc6-bb51-568de66fd7c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b36fbf4d-bb56-53ea-bcd3-bd3fbb7b094e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106070" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{y}{x}=x\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)=x,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{{y}^{1/2}}{x}=x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,z=x\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{2x}\\,z=\\frac{x}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=\\frac{x}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fb6e0b5-50bd-5bc3-9926-8cce1ea815dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{C-{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238740} {:answer/id #uuid "5b195b37-4d20-505c-ae89-b9a443329f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{C-{e}^{x}}{2{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238845} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee3123a-b991-57e4-b166-c66adaa44398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{C-{e}^{2x}}{2{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239299} {:answer/id #uuid "d0593637-ef94-5572-897c-c8ab00cf7d80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{C-2{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239879} {:answer/id #uuid "f02c7ad2-ea02-5ae9-b738-dc45f744f891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2x{e}^{x}}{C-2{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fb6e0b5-50bd-5bc3-9926-8cce1ea815dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{C-{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238740} :answer-field/id #uuid "192366d6-0728-54fb-85fb-3ed3b5b60e0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ad742d4e-8bb3-5b2d-a572-286f9bbe2b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106073" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y={y}^{2}{e}^{x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-1,\\,q(x)={e}^{x},\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-{y}^{-1}={e}^{x}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-z={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z=-{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=1,\\,Q(x)=-{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot (-{e}^{x}) \\\\ {e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z{e}^{x} & =-{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{x}) & =-{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-{e}^{2x}}{2{e}^{x}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1}=\\frac{C-{e}^{2x}}{2{e}^{x}}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{C-{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd114fc0-127b-5ead-b00d-fe9bffb132d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\left(\\frac{2 + x^{3}}{C + x^{2}}\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144120} {:answer/id #uuid "f165fd86-7b5d-5972-b661-153f3789a251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{C - 2x^{2}}{3x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144121} {:answer/id #uuid "0435f5b5-1868-5ec4-ab51-b968a42aecfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{C + 3x^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144122} {:answer/id #uuid "1756d73e-167c-5559-8f61-0cad7f13c45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{2x^{3}}{C - 2x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144123} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8e9606-7e84-5b69-bc8a-f9aeef6bf9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x^{3}}{C - x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144124}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e47c4c86-e1e5-5928-8e04-a5acbcf9617c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "caf692da-64e7-571b-8ecf-524b4723203b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106074" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n$x^{2}\\frac{dy}{dx} = y^{4} - xy$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7400fe2-57e2-5a4e-bded-f9b2de6b23cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144138} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2852ec-dbe6-5b4c-ad88-11e744ebde41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144139} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ca9576-4d88-545f-befd-42ba5b33586a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144140} {:answer/id #uuid "f88c153a-a6e9-58ba-bd4f-06467d0c8b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144141} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdeff55-d770-5e4a-add0-f7f885d99ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144142}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3f84493d-f98d-517e-a5a1-fe871019e01f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144137}] :question/id #uuid "7b913b73-c105-5ba7-b06a-20d353f239e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-108446" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\n1. $y^{′} + x^{2}y = xy^{2}$\n2. $y^{′} + x^{2}y^{2} = xy^{3}$\n3. $y^{′} + x^{2}y = \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab2f4026-36e6-5fbc-833b-decd18f6a835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144144} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4faf50-366b-579d-a717-61a2ca691125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144145} {:answer/id #uuid "015491ea-883d-52af-973e-04ddfc150ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given equations is a Bernoulli differential equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144146} {:answer/id #uuid "72a8162a-08dd-5d0b-805f-010927f5c146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144147} {:answer/id #uuid "771e905b-a148-5e10-8532-569befd71d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144148}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c43c6790-ab66-5b2b-9d5c-3664185f108c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144143}] :question/id #uuid "5064d2f0-3231-54a8-845d-9b0beda86f87" :question/math-academy-id "q-108447" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\n1. $yy^{′} + x^{2}y^{3} = e^{x}y^{4}$\n2. $y^{2}y^{′} + x^{2}y^{3} = e^{x}y^{4}$\n3. $y^{′} + x^{2}\\sin y = x\\cos^{3} y$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "349f818c-cf20-52dc-9e97-0c025ac3a392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238509} {:answer/id #uuid "50ea1908-2fd7-5a72-a62d-e83e75a0136e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{x}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238754} {:answer/id #uuid "7d93a487-2430-58d6-9642-e38fc1ebdfe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{x}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239144} {:answer/id #uuid "884fd422-3560-570a-b65b-552b55c60c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{x}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239240} {:answer/id #uuid "f14373e5-d988-5875-8ac6-9582fc8d6e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "884fd422-3560-570a-b65b-552b55c60c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{x}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239240} :answer-field/id #uuid "9689e5da-04b7-54b3-886d-0a298bc8dbfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "edb9caeb-1ac6-5c8a-b8d9-e751c89dc231" :question/math-academy-id "q-106071" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some integer $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}-y(2x+3{y}^{2})=0\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}-y(2x+3{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}-2xy-3{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}-2xy & =3{y}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}-2{x}^{-1}y & =3{x}^{-2}{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-2{x}^{-1},\\,q(x)=3{x}^{-2},\\,n=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}\\frac{dy}{dx}-2{x}^{-1}{y}^{-2}=3{x}^{-2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-2{y}^{-3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2{x}^{-1}z=3{x}^{-2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{-1}z=-6{x}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=-6{x}^{-2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20139243-a9a4-560d-acc5-15c4919cf194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238332} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6c3a78-79fe-509f-a0a3-7fd88f29faff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238600} {:answer/id #uuid "52cc1be9-4991-5a91-91fa-7a3527a91a46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238768} {:answer/id #uuid "7057f0ac-cd18-513a-b5d8-f94b0dee9790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239024} {:answer/id #uuid "b473f221-aaac-56e6-bcf2-eb9dc5fa9c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b473f221-aaac-56e6-bcf2-eb9dc5fa9c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239633} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d5972f4-febe-5279-a64b-8a127170a62b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7793e790-8241-5316-bdc4-fcf549de3fa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-106072" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transform the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}-y=0\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2} & =y \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y & ={y}^{1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}z=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb9d536d-0e0e-56d0-b075-65f0dfbd2a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461497} {:answer/id #uuid "508f9c1d-ff37-59ea-8879-8c3b43a99d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508f9c1d-ff37-59ea-8879-8c3b43a99d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461498} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05f7a7f-f105-54d3-b92a-8e85aaa18df5" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}\\,y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10df3356-aa72-55c4-bcd3-8b55d0e35022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461499} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3cf18f-98e0-5531-8398-e40d7d3f3583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae3cf18f-98e0-5531-8398-e40d7d3f3583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461500} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a30126-3bf0-5ebf-853d-b9c28b6450dc" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70c6c33b-acc0-53d0-83fb-1320d1026d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461501} {:answer/id #uuid "55465f4e-feef-55e7-aee1-cf9db4d48e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70c6c33b-acc0-53d0-83fb-1320d1026d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461501} :answer-field/id #uuid "a96caab2-f5ca-53aa-b65f-98a419247edb" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x={y}^{6}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f464429f-4905-5c37-b6cf-d2ce0cb09dd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-108911" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}\\,y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\sqrt{x},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=-1.\n$$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,\\,q(x)=-\\sqrt{x},\\,n=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x={y}^{6}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}\\,y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}$ and ${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a2b16ff-480b-5920-a02a-3a1113084ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461503} {:answer/id #uuid "bb654b6e-18b2-515f-a240-33d5be06024d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a2b16ff-480b-5920-a02a-3a1113084ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461503} :answer-field/id #uuid "0248c736-0f29-5188-901a-4d4aa3e4ae2c" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+{x}^{-2}{y}^{3}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462505} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bac7a93d-d937-5618-80f7-910f2907cb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461505} {:answer/id #uuid "6e24f40f-1611-5210-9da6-6cf12584dfe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e24f40f-1611-5210-9da6-6cf12584dfe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461506} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ef8d6f-1e8a-5807-9ad5-6be9ec18aef6" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}-{e}^{x}y={x}^{2}{y}^{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462506} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "399fd328-0dff-5b83-ad3e-6eadc53264ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461507} {:answer/id #uuid "f13ba9c6-fd30-5e83-986a-34fb441fe34e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592