ked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}+\\sqrt{x}y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $q(x){y}^{n}$ terms.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=x{y}^{3}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,n=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244194 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75270618-7af7-5381-9066-6d3469656acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461515} {:answer/id #uuid "67390882-204b-5352-ad1e-ccec65f496a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75270618-7af7-5381-9066-6d3469656acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461515} :answer-field/id #uuid "b208e569-82a8-5d09-9cd4-e626e88672d8" :answer-field/key "${y}^{2}{y}^{′}-x{y}^{5}={y}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b1fb51-971c-5aa9-804d-0ccdfcc7a696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461517} {:answer/id #uuid "c7880ef3-333f-5868-b08a-8422f8cfd792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 175