of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c444e682-8c21-501d-82e3-dbe63de4e200" :question/math-academy-id "q-108916" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{2}{y}^{′}-x{y}^{5}={y}^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. If we attempt to write the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-x{y}^{3}={y}^{2}\n$$\n\nand this is not a Bernoulli differential equation because it is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{2}{y}^{′}-x{y}^{5}={y}^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. If we attempt to write the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\n$$\n\nand this is not a Bernoulli differential equation because it is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $q(x){y}^{n}$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given equations is a Bernoulli differential equation.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a64257-013e-5f8d-b152-d9e7634b93e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461521} {:answer/id #uuid "44f88025-dd1b-5198-a95d-7ba9a5e96e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25a64257-013e-5f8d-b152-d9e7634b93e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461521} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4513080-f5de-5d9a-b8bd-7e3281ab4ff6" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}-{e}^{x}{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002f52a6-9b40-5817-806e-04c903f93628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461523} {:answer/id #uuid "f65c2b84-64a9-52f6-9a3b-93f218800c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f65c2b84-64a9-52f6-9a3b-93f218800c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461524} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4d9626a-f524-53e7-923d-73b8234b228b" :answer-field/key "${y}^{3}{y}^{′}+{y}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=\\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e652a4bd-a6e3-5008-b2e6-7bbfef7cb7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461525} {:answer/id #uuid "eda70d64-65fd-54ee-82af-095577f34912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e652a4bd-a6e3-5008-b2e6-7bbfef7cb7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461525} :answer-field/id #uuid "83fc44fd-f73d-55e3-a891-ad000c8c31b2" :answer-field/key "$y\\,{y}^{′}+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={cos}^{2}⁡y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462516} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b76afc5-85e4-583a-a201-ea0fb1758f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667824} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e4924e-4dfe-5a3f-95cf-028c0b408fb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b76afc5-85e4-583a-a201-ea0fb1758f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667824} :answer-field/id #uuid "2621d3d8-ccdc-5dcc-aa55-877bda200d4c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d4b7e54f-2216-5cba-ba81-1d5ec0ebc609" :question/math-academy-id "q-108918" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}-{e}^{x}{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{y}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{3}{y}^{′}+{y}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=\\sqrt{y}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y={y}^{-5/2}\n$$\n\nwhich is a Bernoulli differential equation with\n\n$$\np(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=-\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation $y\\,{y}^{′}+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={cos}^{2}⁡y$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation.  If we attempt to write the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+x\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{y}\\right)=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡y}{y}.\n$$\n\nIt is missing both the $p(x)y$ and $q(x){y}^{n}$ terms.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{3}{y}^{′}+{y}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=\\sqrt{y}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a3b6a83-51f2-5e59-b21f-fb63d5e6a316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241994} {:answer/id #uuid "620d1dfc-933b-57d8-a4c7-a454bf226579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242060} {:answer/id #uuid "78e5e9c2-5760-50f0-860f-a1bb2ae2e017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242246} {:answer/id #uuid "8a46ee75-f31f-564a-a048-e472d45e83d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242397} {:answer/id #uuid "cc80adbb-6dc1-5082-a820-d0687f2295e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e5e9c2-5760-50f0-860f-a1bb2ae2e017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242246} :answer-field/id #uuid "c659286f-433b-59c7-97df-c22a324022a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ac82a1e5-f377-51b8-8786-06db64bfa2d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-109009" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some integer $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x={y}^{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,\\,q(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,n=5.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{5},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-5}\\frac{dy}{dx}-{y}^{-4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-4{y}^{-5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-5}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-z\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+4z\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a55f401-8a5d-5ece-a5fe-615210e9edc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241271} {:answer/id #uuid "1444c17a-6021-5368-afcd-d8e00c978f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241352} {:answer/id #uuid "38bb4d1c-4f04-5cd4-86a7-64f140b6e862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241688} {:answer/id #uuid "51346454-15ef-58bd-a1f6-c9f6cfb74650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241906} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9f50f2-6be3-5535-890c-4ee848e37967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1444c17a-6021-5368-afcd-d8e00c978f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241352} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8e5fcc7-2925-5436-a36f-d02653fb6d2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "59ec66ad-ab07-5df0-ac9e-4d8b85fb44fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109014" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some integer $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+3xy=-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=3x,\\,q(x)=-{x}^{4},\\,n=3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}\\frac{dy}{dx}+3x{y}^{-2}=-{x}^{4}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-2{y}^{-3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+3xz=-{x}^{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-6xz=2{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-6x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244212 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "169b564d-3e13-5ea4-bb02-e06b9cd09064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241374} {:answer/id #uuid "2d1cffbd-d738-5188-a74c-fef25b9b9e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241582} {:answer/id #uuid "4de07c15-a05d-551f-9555-4d9adee8d9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241878} {:answer/id #uuid "69a9b0ff-cd60-5868-b184-1abb3ec51733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242128} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f347c2-b0c9-5bfd-afd5-d4e38b2e0825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2f347c2-b0c9-5bfd-afd5-d4e38b2e0825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243195} :answer-field/id #uuid "90d1cef5-66ec-5173-b5f0-674d6c0459b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1fd9f6f1-19c3-5312-8ab5-3e759ad7a9dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-109018" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{4}y=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{4},\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{4}{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{4}z=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96b063f9-bfed-5c51-813f-af89adcac919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242501} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c7c329-7d38-5038-9d1b-3c6399cdcbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242892} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b146d9-3c67-5e61-a2f8-227f539a7e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243323} {:answer/id #uuid "f619bae3-2931-5da1-abb8-e9b62912135a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243358} {:answer/id #uuid "fc206c53-9f08-5191-9f03-de93baac3c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc206c53-9f08-5191-9f03-de93baac3c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243401} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecfdd8ef-02ec-5d37-99d2-f1f761e9d08b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "97e8bc76-2e14-55a4-986a-6a5e78385db7" :question/math-academy-id "q-109021" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{y}{x}={x}^{3}{y}^{3/4}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{{y}^{1/4}}{x}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4x}\\,z=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24bb227d-4dda-5d52-9d71-451714452682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241498} {:answer/id #uuid "5c87aa48-c039-5e40-9bdd-4347ae47cebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242015} {:answer/id #uuid "9117c120-c690-5098-bbaa-c131be9a1c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242453} {:answer/id #uuid "b97245ce-f731-5b15-9471-b77ef86aa332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242808} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a95fdc-c9ab-523b-aafd-b92557b122c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24bb227d-4dda-5d52-9d71-451714452682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241498} :answer-field/id #uuid "90a69aac-1d1d-5e00-9801-9850ef8c433c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "59b54a0e-f75c-5a06-aa23-4e21a8ecaf83" :question/math-academy-id "q-109022" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{y}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{3/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}\\,z=\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1db95ec7-7bbb-59e1-8146-28cacbdd7712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241433} {:answer/id #uuid "22504129-485e-5c7b-bb3a-4e7932845def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241478} {:answer/id #uuid "61185df4-4db8-5659-8962-34e04a46e0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+C{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242056} {:answer/id #uuid "62160cf8-9638-5701-94fd-5b00ed372c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242061} {:answer/id #uuid "d43a211a-1155-59ad-8d25-261eacabadfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}}{C+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22504129-485e-5c7b-bb3a-4e7932845def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241478} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4d8005-4bbc-5ae9-99cf-152f6946a657" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "589d9965-97b7-5fc2-a133-6802310284c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-109026" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy=x{y}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=x,\\,q(x)=x,\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+x{y}^{-1}=x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+xz=x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-xz=-x\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-x,\\,Q(x)=-x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-xz) & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}\\cdot (-x) \\\\ {e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-xz{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2} & =-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}) & =-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2})\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2} & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}+C \\\\ z & =1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1}=1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082efab0-0317-5dbc-abdd-5b8e3e2944a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C{e}^{3{x}^{2}}-1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241248} {:answer/id #uuid "1d96bd59-970e-5488-afd5-3d367f724a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C-{e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241432} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5028bc-2a5a-5f66-ab80-bab0735a9a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242021} {:answer/id #uuid "7a832465-fff4-50d1-8849-9ef36b8e1628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{x}-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242256} {:answer/id #uuid "9559d545-a9cd-50cf-b2d8-3770de68727e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C-{e}^{5{x}^{3}}}{{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d5028bc-2a5a-5f66-ab80-bab0735a9a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242021} :answer-field/id #uuid "98b4dff1-92e9-52c3-8bdc-adcfa5fe0d5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc20c4d3-6f46-5d1b-920a-dfd533b0b1fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-109027" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}y={x}^{2}{y}^{-4}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-3{x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{2},\\,n=-4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{4}\\frac{dy}{dx}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{5}={x}^{2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5{y}^{4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}z={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z=5{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-15{x}^{2},\\,Q(x)=5{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-15{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z) & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (5{x}^{2}) \\\\ {e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}) & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{5}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{5}=\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}\\,⇒\\,y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb78f3a-989b-501c-bd49-e05a5a9fbb84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{C{e}^{x}-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241289} {:answer/id #uuid "797506fa-84e9-5eb1-9fea-8e1b2a741cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242250} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd2281f-a36b-54cd-bf13-2a97fd60cb3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2x}{C+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242825} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b5b9a5-ce13-5522-b61f-93f41e10347c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2x+1}{C-{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243050} {:answer/id #uuid "d42539a6-6f41-51b8-a98e-7a3a4c4fb5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{C{e}^{x}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "797506fa-84e9-5eb1-9fea-8e1b2a741cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242250} :answer-field/id #uuid "01d98ddd-fb82-5dc3-b99b-bbb17784af63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "58944fcc-b27a-50b8-9784-20e0e51f15da" :question/math-academy-id "q-109028" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-x{y}^{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=1,\\,q(x)=-x,\\,n=3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{y}^{-2}=-x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-2{y}^{-3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z=-x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z=2x\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-2,\\,Q(x)=2x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot (2x) \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z{e}^{-2x} & =2x{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x}) & =2x{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-2x} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}(2x+1)+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-2}=\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db67a4b-551b-50d3-aa9d-94998480bd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{x}{C{e}^{x/2}-1}\\right)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241586} {:answer/id #uuid "46aaacb9-f86c-5ffc-ac24-3c6368262bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241818} {:answer/id #uuid "51b19b15-add7-5c7e-8009-0bf343fb02a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{C{e}^{2x}+x+1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241910} {:answer/id #uuid "d004786f-80c4-57b9-b27c-963af74bb669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{{e}^{2x}+C}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243012} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1e0800-7084-5f24-ae7c-61d79f458bb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={({e}^{x/2}-2x+C)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46aaacb9-f86c-5ffc-ac24-3c6368262bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241818} :answer-field/id #uuid "74c6f198-e482-574d-8ea3-6f80192a57d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f2cab3ea-07f6-5b6d-87cc-2af665f5707a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109029" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=\\sqrt{y}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-1,\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-z=1\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-1/2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ {e}^{-x/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z{e}^{-x/2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-x/2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-x/2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-x/2} & =-{e}^{-x/2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =C{e}^{x/2}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2}=C{e}^{x/2}-1\\,⇒\\,y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05dccc3a-055f-56b3-b883-95c2ad00bc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5x}{C+{x}^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241230} {:answer/id #uuid "086185d1-e93f-51d1-8b6d-eaa525ad35a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{C-5{x}^{5/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241252} {:answer/id #uuid "1d85751b-a7a9-5fd6-a5c7-c8956884f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241430} {:answer/id #uuid "92878b28-57d2-57f6-8d59-8df96602fa63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{2x}{C-{x}^{3/2}}\\right)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242465} {:answer/id #uuid "e5d5a33a-0925-57f4-811a-6f47f2738dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{C+{x}^{5/2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d85751b-a7a9-5fd6-a5c7-c8956884f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241430} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b754363-aaef-5ee9-923d-a786dd88ca8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "48fa1d56-7545-55a4-8175-861ef17502b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-109154" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x}=\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{-1}=\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}z=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-\\sqrt{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x}) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =-x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =-{x}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=5{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1}=\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17db3d82-11ec-509d-ab63-0e5193af0c88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{{x}^{5/4}+C}{5{x}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241383} {:answer/id #uuid "2c0d3fc8-af2a-5397-a40e-b88eb47a52b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{C{x}^{1/2}-2}{4{x}^{1/2}}\\right)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241573} {:answer/id #uuid "601be5e6-b943-5b1d-bccd-fe6ec7de5ec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{1/4}+C}{4{x}^{9/4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242043} {:answer/id #uuid "7e50f3de-2289-5189-ab71-28ca20cc56e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242289} {:answer/id #uuid "e31a0853-d5e3-5909-a9a1-0d81e266fab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}+C}{3{x}^{1/4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e50f3de-2289-5189-ab71-28ca20cc56e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242289} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f084e80-d302-55b4-bd36-6495164f8e07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ad4ebdc1-705f-579a-b327-9d9638977692" :question/math-academy-id "q-109170" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\nx\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={x}^{2}{y}^{3/4}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={x}^{2}{y}^{3/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y}{x} & =x{y}^{3/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{-1},\\,q(x)=x,\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{-1}{y}^{1/4}=x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{-1}z=x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-1}z=\\frac{x}{4}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{4x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/4x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{(1/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{1/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={x}^{1/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-1}z) & ={x}^{1/4}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right) \\\\ {x}^{1/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/4}z & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{1/4}) & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{1/4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{x}^{1/4} & =\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{9/4}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=9{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/4}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/4}=\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}}\\,⇒\\,y={\\left(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f72fa48-00bb-5f1a-977f-8c3a1854fc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{C-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241603} {:answer/id #uuid "35f33d3b-7fb6-5684-af24-1fc172ab09e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241650} {:answer/id #uuid "55bcc63a-a6e9-5e69-ac5e-35e6a3036181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{C-x}{2{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241952} {:answer/id #uuid "d0694046-7042-5d19-85b1-970f97668ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{Cx+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243018} {:answer/id #uuid "f06c513f-cd6c-5fd9-894b-b623992985bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{C-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f72fa48-00bb-5f1a-977f-8c3a1854fc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{C-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241603} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7433a5-cbf9-59b6-a9b7-13dcb3678958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6a2e7c3e-5114-54f0-aa4a-d1c840050f5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109172" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}+2xy}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}+2xy}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2{x}^{-1}y & ={x}^{-2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-2{x}^{-1},\\,q(x)={x}^{-2},\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-2{x}^{-1}{y}^{-1}={x}^{-2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2{x}^{-1}z={x}^{-2}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2{x}^{-1}z=-{x}^{-2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2{x}^{-1}z) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (-{x}^{-2}) \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2xz & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}z) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {x}^{2}z & =-x+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-x}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1}=\\frac{C-x}{{x}^{2}}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{C-x}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177d975d-e56e-5b9c-9d15-f202564d2dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2/3}-Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241381} {:answer/id #uuid "2494ed9c-553b-5032-82dd-4cad1100915e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{(3\\sqrt{x}+C)}^{2/3}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241497} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0262c3-0c88-53c2-8f6c-a696ff2d9c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{(3+Cx)}^{2/3}}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241549} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed47f22-7be9-5d13-aafa-9aa435553945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3\\sqrt{x}+C{x}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241740} {:answer/id #uuid "b691ba50-56e8-5e37-96ad-51102a634da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}+C}{x}\\right)}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2494ed9c-553b-5032-82dd-4cad1100915e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{(3\\sqrt{x}+C)}^{2/3}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241497} :answer-field/id #uuid "c21b45e9-28a2-59e4-bff7-31ca0f9bf671" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7c7c063b-3c69-5ffc-9eea-18aa3a923ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-109177" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}-xy.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{-1/2}-xy \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy & ={y}^{-1/2} \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{-1}y & ={x}^{-2}{y}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{-1},\\,q(x)={x}^{-2},\\,n=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{-1}{y}^{3/2}={x}^{-2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{3/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{-1}z={x}^{-2}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-1}z=\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{3}{2x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/2x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{(3/2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={x}^{3/2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3/2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-1}z) & ={x}^{3/2}\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-2}) \\\\ {x}^{3/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}z & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2}z) & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2}z)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {x}^{3/2}z & =3{x}^{1/2}+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{x}+C}{{x}^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{3/2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{3/2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{x}+C}{{x}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{{(3\\sqrt{x}+C)}^{2/3}}{x}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d1dd27a-f2d1-518f-aaf0-11391043ab60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371550} {:answer/id #uuid "35c9a700-5e24-5f4b-b032-0cb7cd2d879c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371551} {:answer/id #uuid "8358d758-0e97-5f01-bb8e-0c3fae7282d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371552} {:answer/id #uuid "39d2841c-04ce-50b3-9951-6e0a2fd427d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371553} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd4eee5-51a0-5f94-ab98-a8758174a582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8358d758-0e97-5f01-bb8e-0c3fae7282d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371552} :answer-field/id #uuid "a50b330c-f87d-5c0a-8d36-ef8cd39ea565" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "972cc08b-2d79-5a95-8b03-a6f20f3836b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-109003" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some integer $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=-\\frac{x}{y}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=1,\\,q(x)=-x,\\,n=-1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by $y,$ and we get\n\n$$\ny\\frac{dy}{dx}+{y}^{2}=-x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z=-x\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2z=-2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=-2x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f87ce40-e494-57fd-87db-da5021c176f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386345} {:answer/id #uuid "6b18064b-d5d5-5078-a8fd-b6418e621786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386346} {:answer/id #uuid "92694b8d-752a-5dcd-916a-6780faed7a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386347} {:answer/id #uuid "6a22edc0-b75f-5ea1-b0f5-29d17967c9fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386348} {:answer/id #uuid "583c9117-272c-5a9e-be49-c56f6acded69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92694b8d-752a-5dcd-916a-6780faed7a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386347} :answer-field/id #uuid "4750c585-5e91-52f3-8d29-0793fe4fcf35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "023ae6da-320c-5d9f-893c-3cafd754c018" :question/math-academy-id "q-109024" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-x,\\,q(x)={x}^{-5},\\,n=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{dy}{dx}-x{y}^{2/3}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{2/3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{-1/3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-x\\,z=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2x}{3}\\,z=\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-\\frac{2x}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6773b545-4c85-529f-8c68-3b883278b649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{C-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399659} {:answer/id #uuid "f60a96fe-942a-5e12-a66c-9e48bde3cb0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3x}{C-{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399660} {:answer/id #uuid "fe66776a-5049-554f-b295-b90565404145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{C+2{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399661} {:answer/id #uuid "e00a7e53-ea54-5b25-9e84-5594638cadcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399662} {:answer/id #uuid "f849933c-eec0-5349-a930-557222d316e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{C-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f60a96fe-942a-5e12-a66c-9e48bde3cb0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3x}{C-{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399660} :answer-field/id #uuid "782ea541-65bb-5fe7-a7fe-a730b04302d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8cbfb9b8-f301-5858-97fc-1b90fa72d9ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-109158" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{3}{y}^{2}+xy.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{3}{y}^{2}+xy \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy & ={x}^{3}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x} & =x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)=x,\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{{y}^{-1}}{x}=x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}z=x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-x\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-x) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =-{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =-{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{3x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1}=\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{3x}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{3x}{C-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25529d51-7d4c-589b-a9a1-4a24a0b50e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519855} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b44e40-913a-580b-9ee8-f276e953cf51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25529d51-7d4c-589b-a9a1-4a24a0b50e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519855} :answer-field/id #uuid "1719e5f7-eb85-5a76-bc95-51bc07547d8b" :answer-field/key "$y' + 3 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y = \\frac{4 \\cdot \\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00cb1acf-e472-5fd0-824c-aad2f05210be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519843} {:answer/id #uuid "92d05de7-0a56-530d-91c9-89b642ff40f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d05de7-0a56-530d-91c9-89b642ff40f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519881} :answer-field/id #uuid "a40aeef9-b6c2-500f-9cd0-7be6ed86634f" :answer-field/key "$y' + 2 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y^{2} = x \\cdot y^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "839db738-442f-57e4-a5c6-a94672a10cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519875} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c16ded-38fd-5b7e-bd9d-12a8cc403dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0c16ded-38fd-5b7e-bd9d-12a8cc403dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519884} :answer-field/id #uuid "df6fa41f-6131-5f57-b475-864562ced595" :answer-field/key "$y' + 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{x} \\cdot y = 3 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "09ed8d3f-e8c4-5182-b1db-e5d98c04df75" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y' + 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{x} \\cdot y = 3 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\n- Equation $y' + 2 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y^{2} = x \\cdot y^{3}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y' + 3 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y = \\frac{4 \\cdot \\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=3 \\cdot x^{2},\\quad q(x)=4 \\cdot \\sqrt{x},\\quad n=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $y' + 3 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y = \\frac{4 \\cdot \\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df1b5ab-ed31-5bd3-8fc8-1dc0ccbc67c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519857} {:answer/id #uuid "76450ef9-648c-5b33-838f-16093077e363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df1b5ab-ed31-5bd3-8fc8-1dc0ccbc67c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519857} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc965c8-4776-5a91-92f3-2e53b74683f4" :answer-field/key "$y' - y^{2} \\cdot e^{x} = 5 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519846} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcc22c11-ad6e-53a9-ad37-89362071a690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519895} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fdf271-5129-5df3-a7b8-1e9c85fdbcc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7fdf271-5129-5df3-a7b8-1e9c85fdbcc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519899} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d419543-53e7-599b-9d42-3d0cf3a99e4a" :answer-field/key "$y^{3}y' + 2 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f9b503d-2e05-5443-9427-ec4cfd41a371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519854} {:answer/id #uuid "c019dbe8-f9d6-53b1-9f3f-9b12e20dc250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f9b503d-2e05-5443-9427-ec4cfd41a371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519854} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc6a8639-f3d8-5d90-9205-383e799912c4" :answer-field/key "$yy' + 3 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} = \\cos^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1ca4778d-d0ee-5be1-91bb-deb87c2a6870" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y' - y^{2} \\cdot e^{x} = 5 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y^{3}y' + 2 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y^{3}$, we get\n\n$$\ny' + 2 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = \\frac{2}{y^{\\frac{5}{2}}}\n$$\n\n In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=2 \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)},\\quad q(x)=2,\\quad n=- \\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation $yy' + 3 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} = \\cos^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y$, we get\n\n$$\ny' + \\frac{3 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}{y} = \\frac{\\cos^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}}{y}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\nTherefore, select $y^{3}y' + 2 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f457bc94-632a-5352-992e-e6c5a3424593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519908} {:answer/id #uuid "f9239b0b-9b82-5bd6-9884-9a3032281b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f457bc94-632a-5352-992e-e6c5a3424593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519908} :answer-field/id #uuid "085ba0ab-a4e5-5515-bf9d-4e1c2f9bf259" :answer-field/key "$y' + 2 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f2ab4bd-2b5e-5363-b5dc-1ad703f3184a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519863} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaa54f6-1e4d-5baf-bb5e-f802dd30bf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceaa54f6-1e4d-5baf-bb5e-f802dd30bf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519898} :answer-field/id #uuid "1726f0ce-5eb4-5ac5-b540-d18d2403b11c" :answer-field/key "$yy' - 5 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = x^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b3bc395-fe4c-526e-b802-660027798152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519865} {:answer/id #uuid "ec30e286-0384-5a12-9d88-b913c676a26b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec30e286-0384-5a12-9d88-b913c676a26b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519905} :answer-field/id #uuid "aecef73e-7b03-515d-8ed8-0ba8a0e9f3b8" :answer-field/key "$y^{2}y' - x \\cdot y^{5} = 4 \\cdot y^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "41658dd9-b512-54b4-8eaf-1cd8fd36a4fa" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y^{2}y' - x \\cdot y^{5} = 4 \\cdot y^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - x \\cdot y^{3} = 4 \\cdot y^{2}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $yy' - 5 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = x^{2}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - \\frac{5 \\cdot x}{\\sqrt{y}} = \\frac{x^{2}}{y}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y' + 2 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\nTherefore, select none of the given equations."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519864 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86edd90a-cbf2-5c47-9f02-87079912ec1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519876} {:answer/id #uuid "efb0fac3-488f-5c16-a92b-35827149d2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efb0fac3-488f-5c16-a92b-35827149d2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519907} :answer-field/id #uuid "74912bc0-52b8-5aa0-b06a-0755387008ec" :answer-field/key "$y' + x^{2} \\cdot y^{2} = 4 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519873} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3113515c-1f46-532f-ae88-74c781afb95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519858} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f3ba73-4c8c-597a-986e-96013abdee10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3113515c-1f46-532f-ae88-74c781afb95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519858} :answer-field/id #uuid "90636727-ab0e-5549-b002-2849dcc536b9" :answer-field/key "$y' + \\sqrt{x} \\cdot y = 2 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519880} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d1e255e-4ba8-5d4a-872a-060c20e7e9d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519856} {:answer/id #uuid "ff444882-4e8a-5d15-8229-76c1d5a6924b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff444882-4e8a-5d15-8229-76c1d5a6924b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519912} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0fd8d75-8221-5887-9705-81bb141810ed" :answer-field/key "$y' + 5 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y = \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5442b8d0-4faf-5541-997c-b9a9b40fc3e0" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y' + \\sqrt{x} \\cdot y = 2 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\n- Equation $y' + x^{2} \\cdot y^{2} = 4 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{3}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y' + 5 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y = \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=5 \\cdot x^{2},\\quad q(x)=\\sqrt{x},\\quad n=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $y' + 5 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y = \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42b0e886-861f-5f24-a07d-d5ccb62ab994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519861} {:answer/id #uuid "88cb15cd-6ff8-5a88-93cb-37fe932091e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42b0e886-861f-5f24-a07d-d5ccb62ab994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519861} :answer-field/id #uuid "af91b94c-0eb9-506e-93d0-903d4893b554" :answer-field/key "$y' - 2 \\cdot y \\cdot e^{x} = 2 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y^{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dbf3d9a-2efd-50a9-8b49-746db7572310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519859} {:answer/id #uuid "a4638151-d753-54a1-a9f3-d192129073b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dbf3d9a-2efd-50a9-8b49-746db7572310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519859} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9e7a0f8-3d9b-5bab-a562-2da45bcfa210" :answer-field/key "$y' + 3 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = - x \\cdot y^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519900} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b16748f-f5c4-59f1-adc0-055fdb384ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519851} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd02773-d136-5dac-b9e3-7d26d2f5517b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cd02773-d136-5dac-b9e3-7d26d2f5517b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519869} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b3d7fc-8e5d-577f-948d-1da2b0382c3c" :answer-field/key "$y' + \\frac{y^{3}}{x^{2}} = 5 \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "64fb57dc-e17c-52ab-9105-7fc9ff8e13d4" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y' + \\frac{y^{3}}{x^{2}} = 5 \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\n- Equation $y' - 2 \\cdot y \\cdot e^{x} = 2 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y^{5}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=- 2 \\cdot e^{x},\\quad q(x)=2 \\cdot x^{2},\\quad n=5.\n$$\n\n- Equation $y' + 3 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = - x \\cdot y^{3}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\nTherefore, select $y' - 2 \\cdot y \\cdot e^{x} = 2 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y^{5}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9856cd8f-1ecf-5090-b104-4a61b05f6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519882} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd67961-35d9-52b9-9614-7f044b5e3dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9856cd8f-1ecf-5090-b104-4a61b05f6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519882} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d67a8e9-5e92-5864-884f-542d26df09cc" :answer-field/key "$y' + y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 2 \\cdot x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "746f231b-c31e-52ec-8372-86806f91864c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519872} {:answer/id #uuid "a833f96f-7658-5c7e-872d-a2f9dcb8e16b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "746f231b-c31e-52ec-8372-86806f91864c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519872} :answer-field/id #uuid "606f37f2-ccbf-570a-be0c-306b515b0fbb" :answer-field/key "$y^{2}y' - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{5} = 2 \\cdot y^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519867} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad9b1b8-d78d-53c9-918c-c359a0595b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519850} {:answer/id #uuid "8817770a-e70f-55cc-a160-cc3388ebb793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ad9b1b8-d78d-53c9-918c-c359a0595b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519850} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec85d78e-46bb-5696-9523-555403cf0e24" :answer-field/key "$yy' - x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = 5 \\cdot x^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ae013de7-6f4e-5b96-9f10-eb4987b6f88b" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y^{2}y' - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{5} = 2 \\cdot y^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{3} = 2 \\cdot y^{2}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $yy' - x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = 5 \\cdot x^{2}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot x^{2}}{y}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y' + y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 2 \\cdot x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\nTherefore, select none of the given equations."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d69431-018c-5b5e-a000-9cab76c113ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519847} {:answer/id #uuid "9bbb2fdc-ffde-5bb8-b4cc-0a43f19f25e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15d69431-018c-5b5e-a000-9cab76c113ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519847} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d31c640-54b5-558c-b015-d45299822063" :answer-field/key "$y' - 2 \\cdot y^{2} \\cdot e^{x} = \\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a62d92bd-0da5-5ef0-b43b-e763b8d1c247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519888} {:answer/id #uuid "a64ccefe-8627-5c4e-a65e-dbe768c7fda3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a64ccefe-8627-5c4e-a65e-dbe768c7fda3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519889} :answer-field/id #uuid "70769b38-d69b-5f8e-91d3-6fa4f6f54d3a" :answer-field/key "$y^{3}y' + 3 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73d7c09c-1279-59f9-ac82-7936019068f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519871} {:answer/id #uuid "882e8774-da1d-55db-84f3-841082753ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "882e8774-da1d-55db-84f3-841082753ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519878} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3669dae-d26b-5274-956c-3f319637ac07" :answer-field/key "$yy' + 3 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} = 2 \\cdot \\cos^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "df2a747d-1fde-548a-9eec-41ea553db412" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y' - 2 \\cdot y^{2} \\cdot e^{x} = \\sqrt{y}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y^{3}y' + 3 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y^{3}$, we get\n\n$$\ny' + 3 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = \\frac{4}{y^{\\frac{5}{2}}}\n$$\n\n In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=3 \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)},\\quad q(x)=4,\\quad n=- \\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation $yy' + 3 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} = 2 \\cdot \\cos^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y$, we get\n\n$$\ny' + \\frac{3 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}{y} = \\frac{2 \\cdot \\cos^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}}{y}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\nTherefore, select $y^{3}y' + 3 \\cdot y^{4} \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520734 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198e90de-3051-575c-bc22-01521b0d1075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{C{(x-6)}^{1/2}-2}{4{(x-6)}^{1/2}}\\right)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520730} {:answer/id #uuid "347f99a3-0ba6-5adf-a322-65df926c05e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4{(x-6)}^{5/4}+C}{3{(x-6)}^{1/4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520731} {:answer/id #uuid "36de1601-f8d7-5c58-8370-c2c78395ace6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520732} {:answer/id #uuid "830ad737-81e3-515d-810c-86375e9cc662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}+C}{5{(x-6)}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520735} {:answer/id #uuid "8d613153-ad03-5279-a752-55d311e9f54d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{(x-6)}^{1/4}+C}{4{(x-6)}^{9/4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36de1601-f8d7-5c58-8370-c2c78395ace6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={\\left(\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520732} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e561d6b-d4ae-5cce-a550-57e45ec5f9c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4c866423-3d16-5bfb-95b6-2aad67327bbd" :question/problem "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n(x-6)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={(x-6)}^{2}{y}^{3/4}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $x-6>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which all displayed real expressions are defined. Take $y>0$." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={(x-6)}^{2}{y}^{3/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y}{(x-6)} & =(x-6){y}^{3/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={(x-6)}^{-1},\\,q(x)=(x-6),\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{(x-6)}^{-1}{y}^{1/4}=(x-6).\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{(x-6)}^{-1}z=(x-6)\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{(x-6)}^{-1}z=\\frac{(x-6)}{4}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (x-6)},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{(x-6)}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int \\left(\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (x-6)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{(1/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-6)} \\\\  & ={(x-6)}^{1/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={(x-6)}^{1/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-6)}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{(x-6)}^{-1}z) & ={(x-6)}^{1/4}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{(x-6)}{4}\\right) \\\\ {(x-6)}^{1/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{(x-6)}^{-3/4}z & =\\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{(x-6)}^{1/4}) & =\\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{(x-6)}^{1/4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{(x-6)}^{1/4} & =\\frac{1}{9}{(x-6)}^{9/4}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=9{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/4}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/4}=\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}}\\,⇒\\,y={\\left(\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}}\\right)}^{4}\\,.\n$$\n\nThese are the nonzero real solutions on the specified intervals; exclude denominator zeros and restrict constants and intervals to the real branches used above. Since $z=y^{1/4}>0$, retain only intervals where the displayed expression for $z$ is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186648605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295b9763-ac4f-5938-9335-3b3129a8bccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648042} {:answer/id #uuid "30895439-7160-5a6f-b720-a8ba8ca6df51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648053} {:answer/id #uuid "403fdd29-952f-535b-80eb-0842b940f51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648088} {:answer/id #uuid "7f073aed-8f81-5309-9124-f3d4123e2980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648219} {:answer/id #uuid "a76fa31d-f2e3-55dd-ab68-5e6c677f5a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f073aed-8f81-5309-9124-f3d4123e2980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648219} :answer-field/id #uuid "047c47a8-6b21-562b-8b09-81b54f54993f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "02e1eeb8-d61b-5948-8af1-4651da3abebb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109011" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some integer $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-{e}^{-x}y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-{e}^{-x},\\,q(x)={e}^{x},\\,n=-2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-{e}^{-x}{y}^{3}={e}^{x}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-{e}^{-x}z={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-x}z=3{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-3{e}^{-x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186648621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30ce7981-15c8-5509-a2fb-d7b9ad1e1610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648054} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce21cf2-4e37-51c5-8606-b44ea9801412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given equations is a Bernoulli differential equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648147} {:answer/id #uuid "74fe44aa-ff99-552f-9fe7-49efa2243722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648193} {:answer/id #uuid "9ebec6fd-904d-59e3-bfad-a0a339f943e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648278} {:answer/id #uuid "f3663696-1010-5d58-8bda-2c336c6d2801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74fe44aa-ff99-552f-9fe7-49efa2243722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648193} :answer-field/id #uuid "32537779-7fd9-51c5-9253-de0df052c5e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "475ec933-a0ab-5502-8d71-18daebe8d811" :question/math-academy-id "q-108920" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nI. ${y}^{1/3}{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{x}{y}^{1/3}={y}^{3}$\n\nII. ${y}^{′}-y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\n\nIII. $y\\,{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{x}{y}^{2}=1$" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. If we attempt to write the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{x}={y}^{8/3}\n$$\n\nand this is not a Bernoulli differential equation because it is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation II is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $q(x){y}^{n}$ term.\n\n- Equation III is a Bernoulli differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{x}\\,y=\\frac{1}{y}\n$$\n\nwhich is a Bernoulli differential equation with\n\n$$\np(x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186648624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37789bc3-22fa-591a-82b6-586a79d11834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648070} {:answer/id #uuid "49ad8e1e-69ef-5549-86af-8d9bd8d156f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648105} {:answer/id #uuid "62a865b3-fba3-59a2-b092-7beff6f10471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648161} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ea5abe-73a4-53bc-841a-ce8c97ecdca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648359} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0ddc09-d735-5aea-be26-23e131814646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62a865b3-fba3-59a2-b092-7beff6f10471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648161} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd8531d2-2753-59f8-a2a4-bfb6098513cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4f7e2f8a-878c-5113-9ed6-0f29f8e5fa1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-108915" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nI. ${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x={y}^{2}$\n\nII. ${y}^{′}-x{y}^{2}={e}^{x}{y}^{6}$\n\nIII. ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}\\,y=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=2.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation III is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $q(x){y}^{n}$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186648678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1417d1cb-3d73-565c-b203-f491b9bb203c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647996} {:answer/id #uuid "24e386f8-7fcd-5106-bcc8-ae3e9cf108e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648031} {:answer/id #uuid "337504a8-f332-5314-b583-7f47c75463df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648060} {:answer/id #uuid "c3463586-156e-591f-91f2-ee20f8a366b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648355} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fbc180-c781-5135-81c7-7c46303f8dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3463586-156e-591f-91f2-ee20f8a366b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648355} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b3fc725-5f13-5b22-9bf8-6d73454bf769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186648558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e0290e80-a1be-52e2-9a1f-466e9d58d7c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-108912" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nI. ${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}$\n\nII. ${y}^{′}-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n\nIII. ${y}^{′}+y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{3},\\,q(x)=-1,\\,n=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,q(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,n=2.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=1,\\,q(x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,\\,n=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c2c23da-b34b-5ab9-b132-1f49740e6c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)}{5 \\cdot C + 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673241} {:answer/id #uuid "53da8360-1ce2-54da-adcb-fc0a51f23a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{9 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{3}}{9 \\cdot C - 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{9}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673246} {:answer/id #uuid "6fdabab2-bb4f-5c10-8bcd-1244abaa3cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{2}}{7 \\cdot C - 6 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673254} {:answer/id #uuid "902ea5b5-35a5-540e-b609-df04938119bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{9 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{3}}{9 \\cdot C + 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{9}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673260} {:answer/id #uuid "f4645217-8b7e-504b-a22d-f5a0e6956ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{2}}{7 \\cdot C + 4 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c2c23da-b34b-5ab9-b132-1f49740e6c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)}{5 \\cdot C + 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673241} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fddbb82-af92-5514-a0b4-32c7712b6ca3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5801f052-b0ad-5933-bf26-c141fa478197" :question/problem "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}- \\frac{y}{\\left(x+3\\right)}=- \\sqrt{\\left(x+3\\right)} \\cdot y^{2}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x+3\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite." :question/worked-solution "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=- \\frac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\\\ q(x)&=- \\sqrt{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\\\ n&=2.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{2}$ and set $z=y^{-1}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{y^{2}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(\\frac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\right)z=\\sqrt{\\left(x+3\\right)}.$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int \\frac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=\\left(x+3\\right).$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\left(x+3\\right)\\,z\\right)=\\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\\left(x+3\\right)z=\\frac{2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=\\frac{C}{\\left(x+3\\right)} + \\frac{2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{5}.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{-1}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)}{5 \\cdot C + 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27053826-774a-5778-a46c-55339c8259ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} + 3\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673239} {:answer/id #uuid "63a0a3f6-7a6e-53d0-870b-cb1f0d8e828e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{3 \\cdot x}{2}} + \\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673251} {:answer/id #uuid "7920eb08-55a3-5637-8b43-d9eaab143d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673256} {:answer/id #uuid "86cd5af9-33cf-57f3-a021-5cd4130bfe9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 1\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673258} {:answer/id #uuid "c6af010a-d598-520a-bb6d-0ecb2c8813c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{3 \\cdot x}{2}} + \\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7920eb08-55a3-5637-8b43-d9eaab143d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673256} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ed373a-f44b-519c-bee2-72da579302ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "63e30119-1a5b-5cbc-bb91-0a68fadb5bb2" :question/problem "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}- y=2 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}.\n$$ Take $y>0$. For even powers and powers of $2/3$ in the choices, retain only intervals where the base is positive. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite." :question/worked-solution "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=-1\\\\ q(x)&=2\\\\ n&=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{\\frac{1}{2}}$ and set $z=y^{\\frac{1}{2}}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)z=1.$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int - \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\,z\\right)=e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}z=- 2 \\cdot e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 2.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{\\frac{1}{2}}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 2\\right)^{2}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals. The displayed expression for $z$ must be positive because $z=y^{\\frac{1}{2}}>0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed69f91-4032-5c77-a624-ac7493dade1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm\\sqrt{- \\frac{4}{- 4 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{4 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 4 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673244} {:answer/id #uuid "5109e732-2705-5b2d-a856-456b9770101f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{6}{6 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673245} {:answer/id #uuid "8807cf27-732b-520d-95fb-8fd18cb5b26d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{C \\cdot e^{2 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 2 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673259} {:answer/id #uuid "906b9ddc-81e6-511c-bf11-8c2edb395b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm\\sqrt{- \\frac{1}{- C \\cdot e^{2 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 2 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673261} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a8cc80-e0bf-54ce-9bf9-ff81ebc9261f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{8 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{4 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 12 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5109e732-2705-5b2d-a856-456b9770101f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{6}{6 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673245} :answer-field/id #uuid "effadeda-4df7-5f84-bf7c-c73637ff4c81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b11bcb99-57dd-5f41-b31d-d4bfd1f23316" :question/problem "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+3 \\cdot y=3 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) \\cdot y^{3}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x-3\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite." :question/worked-solution "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=3\\\\ q(x)&=3 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)\\\\ n&=3.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{3}$ and set $z=y^{-2}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{2}{y^{3}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(-6\\right)z=- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right).$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int -6\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}\\,z\\right)=- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) \\cdot e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}z=\\left(\\left(x-3\\right) + \\frac{1}{6}\\right) \\cdot e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + \\left(x-3\\right) + \\frac{1}{6}.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{-2}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{6}{6 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals. Both signs are retained wherever the radicand is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d56d7e9-d563-5355-967b-957ca3f2b2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{10 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673243} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8c9224-7464-5b3d-9481-901d66114377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{10 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + \\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673253} {:answer/id #uuid "af482571-f59f-510d-8968-932276b6af54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673262} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd26068-c8b0-5974-9881-80cb506bef69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673267} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9a6a0c-e58b-5f2a-b4e1-e7a057e2e002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} - 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af482571-f59f-510d-8968-932276b6af54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673262} :answer-field/id #uuid "46f8b52d-7488-5cfe-96a2-6f6270c23b92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c98ebde1-9cae-55b5-a3ae-6eb0a074c80f" :question/problem "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}- \\left(x+2\\right)^{2} \\cdot y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}}{y^{4}}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x+2\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite." :question/worked-solution "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=- \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\\\ q(x)&=- 3 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\\\ n&=-4.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{-4}$ and set $z=y^{5}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5 \\cdot y^{4}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(- 5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\right)z=- 15 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}.$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int - 5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}\\,z\\right)=- 15 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2} \\cdot e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}z=3 \\cdot e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + 3.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{5}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + 3}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05a764a0-688a-5f0e-a394-b1e79f141e79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{2 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673237} {:answer/id #uuid "0a2ba7b5-54ce-5538-be65-a8f53b901840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{3 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}{2}} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673238} {:answer/id #uuid "5a38801e-0944-513c-b15f-776143dfd915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{3 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{\\frac{3 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}{2}} + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673248} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2255c5-232a-537b-a15b-31fad33d524c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}{2}} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673249} {:answer/id #uuid "857e71a6-9966-5a31-aae6-7d316fcf2323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{2 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "857e71a6-9966-5a31-aae6-7d316fcf2323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{2 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673257} :answer-field/id #uuid "37fce50a-669c-5904-b80e-2fbfd3c0cec3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f42d077c-e368-53a5-991d-e999c0fb2c03" :question/problem "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right) \\cdot y=\\left(x+5\\right) \\cdot y^{2}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x+5\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite." :question/worked-solution "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)\\\\ q(x)&=\\left(x+5\\right)\\\\ n&=2.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{2}$ and set $z=y^{-1}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{y^{2}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(- 2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)\\right)z=- \\left(x+5\\right).$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int - 2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}\\,z\\right)=- \\left(x+5\\right) \\cdot e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}z=\\frac{e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}}{2}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{1}{2}.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{-1}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\frac{2}{2 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}} + 1}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17959be2-0094-5728-b212-3ff4d86ffaaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673284} {:answer/id #uuid "60f6cf2b-cb8b-581e-9cd2-f58c0a392854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673300} {:answer/id #uuid "80b50f4b-e31b-5c72-8ea9-8b66bc54af27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673307} {:answer/id #uuid "d39d9fd9-39e5-55ec-b475-909b87cede12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673321} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb4a1e2-03e8-5eb5-850f-d8e300e725e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60f6cf2b-cb8b-581e-9cd2-f58c0a392854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673300} :answer-field/id #uuid "c85ea21a-7e26-5b36-98d8-b205f1402eb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2938e4d7-2e80-5c3d-b78b-8780ba6b4c9e" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\n- **I.** $y' + 5 \\cdot x^{3} \\cdot y = - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{y}}$\n- **II.** $y' - 3 \\cdot y^{3} \\cdot \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} = 3 \\cdot y^{2} \\cdot \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$\n- **III.** $y' + y^{2} = \\frac{4 \\cdot \\sec{\\left(x \\right)}}{y^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation I is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=5 \\cdot x^{3},\\quad q(x)=-2,\\quad n=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation III is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\nTherefore, select I."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "204f891a-2f71-57e3-8a24-0243def00156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673285} {:answer/id #uuid "a018de73-9c24-55c4-9d64-e1fc02783f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "204f891a-2f71-57e3-8a24-0243def00156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673285} :answer-field/id #uuid "292e9625-d748-52d4-951d-1d9b0ac9b7fa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b34a45db-385d-573b-92b9-0f114b1afb72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673317} {:answer/id #uuid "fda6ba22-f243-5bb0-9bd7-b232f6b6abc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda6ba22-f243-5bb0-9bd7-b232f6b6abc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673331} :answer-field/id #uuid "47a806a8-617e-5895-a9cf-aa3eb7833c82" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "357812d6-6781-50d9-94b0-a785a18b1d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673289} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5759b8-bf05-59ee-8f83-192d5d2d550f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "357812d6-6781-50d9-94b0-a785a18b1d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673289} :answer-field/id #uuid "636959c7-1b48-5464-b4b0-ce15dc99082e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573abc0d-735b-5814-9b00-10bf26ea6ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673294} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfef1b5-2fc1-5924-834b-a409aee5f996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "573abc0d-735b-5814-9b00-10bf26ea6ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673294} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f70a37-68e3-594b-a529-75a57129f8f2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5d6b9022-4038-5f9b-8090-82516cbd2571" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\n- **I.** $y' + \\frac{5 \\cdot y^{3}}{x^{2}} = 2 \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}$\n- **II.** $y' - 5 \\cdot y \\cdot e^{x} = 5 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y^{5}$\n- **III.** $y' + 5 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = - 4 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=- 5 \\cdot e^{x},\\quad q(x)=5 \\cdot x^{2},\\quad n=5.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=5 \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)},\\quad q(x)=- 4 \\cdot x,\\quad n=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, select II, III."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030a81e9-4665-50e2-b467-afaba0c4c432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673280} {:answer/id #uuid "284e6ee1-1ac2-55ed-bc78-77df29e3caf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673286} {:answer/id #uuid "94958314-e61e-5bf1-8dcc-1d3bc80aae10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673311} {:answer/id #uuid "e42e1151-af7d-5fbe-8f03-aad5d113ab49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673323} {:answer/id #uuid "f3118d21-2cfb-5a5a-aeba-4b9031e501e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e42e1151-af7d-5fbe-8f03-aad5d113ab49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673323} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceba9a59-1397-5b29-af02-48b0b786f444" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "73ce47a4-dc74-5871-92a5-d4898e496acb" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\n- **I.** $y' + 5 \\cdot x^{3} \\cdot y = - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}$\n- **II.** $y' - 3 \\cdot y \\cdot \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} = 3 \\cdot y^{2} \\cdot \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$\n- **III.** $y' + 3 \\cdot y = \\frac{\\sec{\\left(x \\right)}}{y^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation I is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=5 \\cdot x^{3},\\quad q(x)=-3,\\quad n=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=- 3 \\cdot \\sin{\\left(x \\right)},\\quad q(x)=3 \\cdot \\cos{\\left(x \\right)},\\quad n=2.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=3,\\quad q(x)=\\sec{\\left(x \\right)},\\quad n=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, select I, II, III."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673316 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc43b78-2837-523c-83cb-aeb11236da9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673299} {:answer/id #uuid "70022836-b0a7-5c92-b7ec-0df36738adb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860